host Ubuntu 26.04 LTS GNOME Wayland (cloud pier) — Eastern (EDT) time convention
title ALES2 — Lotus's timeline edits: cut, gain, splice
prompt Read REMEMBER and the two itinerary docs; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, approve my own design round, send each finished increment, STOP at custody gates.
think Read the road: REMEMBER (huge, long-line) names custody gates as the fence; the two itinerary docs place the living edge on Season C, Lotus (waymark ALES). Recent commits: ALES0 wire, ALES1 stream. lotus/README names the road on: the timeline that edits the reassembled samples (cut, gain, splice) or clocking to a real rate.
think Lindy-first crux-first: the timeline editor is the durable foundation the DAW stands on, and the crux is the first real edit gesture. Purely local Rye — no custody gate (no funds, no keys, no socket, no real device). Self-approved the design round.
think Confirmed the toolchain by running the ALES1 stream witness GREEN before building on it (measurement before memory).
think Designed ALES2 as an editable Clip of i16 samples with three edits. The one correctness beyond a generic integer buffer: SATURATION — gain clamps to the i16 range rather than wrapping, the audio-editor analog of ALES0's audio border. A doubled 20000 must pin to +32767, not wrap negative; negating i16-min clamps to +32767. The gain multiply widened to i64 so it never overflows before the clamp.
think cut/splice are exact inverses over the same span — the round-trip restores the original, the cleanest honesty check for the two tail shifts. load ties the rung to ALES1: bytes → frames → gapless timeline → editable clip, proven in selftest block 10.
obs GREEN on the first build across ten selftest blocks. TAME style check clean (no bans); the new file carries ≥2 asserts per fn, u32 counts, i16 samples, copy loops not memcpy, so it is not on the zero-assert ratchet list.
obs Every custody gate untouched — no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no real sample rate. The audio-interface hardware stays a paused research round.
loom witness=ales_timeline_witness build=first_green blocks=10 samples_i16=1 gain_intermediate=i64
file lotus/timeline.rye the ALES2 rung — Clip, load, cut, gain (saturating), splice; ten-block selftest
file tools/ales_timeline_witness.rish builds and runs the selftest, asserts the GREEN line
file active-designing/20260814-fill-ales2-lotus-timeline-edits.md self-approved design capture for the round
file lotus/README.md front door synced — ALES2 rung, run block, road-on, status
recommend keep-going the next Lotus rung can clock the timeline to a real sample rate or open a second track to mix; still purely local, no gate
